ussia, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5bed9d39a641447d13bd6b033b870dbee08c7a480dd54ce67069e74d3496d00</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753--1c825a485886.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
